// Spotlight search words for your apps.
//
// Spotlight already knows an app's name, its GenericName and the Keywords its
// .desktop file ships, plus a built-in table of synonyms living in
// ~/.config/omarchy/plugins/henri.menu/AppAliases.js ("notes" finds Omawrite,
// "photoshop" finds Pinta, "dateien" finds Files).
//
// This file adds your own on top. Every key is a desktop id without the
// .desktop suffix (`obsidian`, `org.gnome.Nautilus`) or the app's visible name
// ("Files"); every value is the list of words that should also find it. The
// file is watched, so a save takes effect on the next keystroke.
//
// A word written with a leading "-" removes one of the built-in ones again:
//
//   {
//     "obsidian": ["zweitgehirn", "tagebuch"],
//     "com.github.PintaProject.Pinta": ["-photoshop"],
//     "code": ["arbeit", "projekt"]
//   }
//
// Whole-line // comments and trailing commas are fine; anything else is JSON.
{
}
